    ],
    "word_count": 50,
    "html": "<p>Robert Brockman was an American software entrepreneur who founded Universal Computer Services to serve car dealerships. A University of Florida business graduate and former Ford and IBM employee, he expanded the company internationally. Its acquisition of Reynolds and Reynolds made him chairman and chief executive of the combined dealership-software business.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Robert Brockman taught himself to program after leaving IBM. His early service sent car dealers weekly printed reports showing their parts inventories. He later developed systems that let owners combine the financial accounts of several dealerships, making it easier to see the business as a whole.\n\nHe also backed young technology companies through the GOOSE Society of Texas. At Rice University’s business-plan competition, he joined Jack Gill in presenting the grand prize to NuMat Technologies, a Northwestern University team developing materials for gas storage. The society contributed investment capital to a wider award combining equity finance, business services and mentoring.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 93,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Detailed independent reporting and a contemporary primary competition account support the two distinct dimensions."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S3",
      "S4"
    ],
    "word_count": 100,
    "html": "<p>Robert Brockman taught himself to program after leaving IBM. His early service sent car dealers weekly printed reports showing their parts inventories. He later developed systems that let owners combine the financial accounts of several dealerships, making it easier to see the business as a whole.</p>\r\n<p>He also backed young technology companies through the GOOSE Society of Texas. At Rice University’s business-plan competition, he joined Jack Gill in presenting the grand prize to NuMat Technologies, a Northwestern University team developing materials for gas storage. The society contributed investment capital to a wider award combining equity finance, business services and mentoring.</p>\r\n"
  },
